<section>
  <p class="eyebrow">Docs</p>
  <h1>Schemas</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Design Lasagna publishes JSON Schemas for its format versions. Each schema
    is available as a raw JSON file and as an npm package
    (<code>@designlasagna/schemas</code>).
  </p>

  <aside class="schema-version-note">
    <p>
      <strong>Format version ≠ package version.</strong> <code>v0.4</code>
      names the schema <em>format</em> — the JSON files served under
      <code>/schemas/v0.4/</code>. The npm package
      <code>@designlasagna/schemas</code> has its own independent release
      version: <code>0.4.0</code> is the package release that ships the v0.4
      format files. Use the format version in <code>$schema</code> URLs, and
      pin the package version when installing.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <h2>v0.4 <span class="version-status">Current · default</span></h2>
  <p>
    v0.4 is the current and default schema format. The v0.4 DTCG token
    extensions, tokens, utilities, icons, and components reference pages are
    published; the remaining v0.4 reference page is not published yet, so
    that entry links straight to the raw contract; see
    <a href="/tools/schemas/">About Schemas</a> for how the format fits
    together.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/schemas/v0.4/dtcg-extensions/">DTCG token extensions</a> —
      optional Design Lasagna governance metadata authored in DTCG
      <code>$extensions</code>
      (<a href="/schemas/v0.4/dtcg-extensions.json">v0.4/dtcg-extensions.json</a>)
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/schemas/v0.4/tokens/">Tokens</a> — the resolved token
      manifest format (<a href="/schemas/v0.4/tokens.json">v0.4/tokens.json</a>)
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/schemas/v0.4/utilities/">Utilities</a> — the utilities
      manifest format (<a href="/schemas/v0.4/utilities.json">v0.4/utilities.json</a>)
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/schemas/v0.4/icons/">Icons</a> — the icons manifest
      format (<a href="/schemas/v0.4/icons.json">v0.4/icons.json</a>)
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/schemas/v0.4/components/">Components</a> — lifecycle
      extensions for Custom Elements Manifest entries
      (<a href="/schemas/v0.4/cem-extensions.json">v0.4/cem-extensions.json</a>)
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/schemas/v0.4/lifecycle.json">Lifecycle</a> — composable
      lifecycle fragments referenced from the other v0.4 contracts
      (<code>v0.4/lifecycle.json</code>)
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>v0.3 <span class="version-status">Previous · compatibility</span></h2>
  <p>
    v0.3 is the previous schema format. Its references remain published for
    systems that still target v0.3 contracts.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/schemas/v0.3/dtcg-extensions/">DTCG token extensions</a> — optional
      Design Lasagna metadata authored in DTCG <code>$extensions</code>
      (<code>v0.3/dtcg-extensions.json</code>)
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/schemas/v0.3/tokens/">Tokens</a> — the tokens manifest
      format (<code>v0.3/tokens.json</code>)
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/schemas/v0.3/utilities/">Utilities</a> — the utilities
      manifest format (<code>v0.3/utilities.json</code>)
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/schemas/v0.3/components/">Components</a> — CEM extensions
      for adding lifecycle metadata to component manifests
      (<code>v0.3/cem-extensions.json</code>)
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
